{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "motion_planning",
    tag: "v1",
    description: [
      "Plans joint paths for the robot's arms that avoid the objects of the planning scene and, where the implementer reads a depth camera, what the camera has seen; checks paths from other sources; and holds the planning scene. Nothing moves: run a path with limb_motion's execute_joint_path. Every plan and check covers the path that move runs, its corners cut as it cuts them. Poses are in the robot frame of limb_motion, positions in meters, orientations unit quaternions [x, y, z, w]; an orientation whose norm lies within 0.001 of 1 is normalized, and any other is refused with rejected. Joint names, their order and their limits are limb_state's and limb_motion's; joint positions are in rad, or m for a prismatic joint. A position where an arm stands is the newest that limb_state reported. The joints of the arms the call does not name, and every gripper's joints, stay where they stand. A joint vector left empty is not given.",
      "The voxel map: a depth ray frees the space it passes through and marks the cube it ends in occupied; space never seen counts as empty; a point on the robot's own body, or inside an object or an attached object, each grown by the implementer's padding, marks nothing and clears the cube it ends in, even when another point of the same frame ends there; adding, moving or attaching an object clears every cube it intersects where the call leaves it. With a camera, plans, Cartesian paths and checks that check collisions are refused with precondition_failed until a depth frame arrives after the implementer starts, and again after each clear_occupancy_map.",
      "A state is the joint positions of the named arms at one instant of the path, the arms at their k-th waypoints together. Each state keeps the clearance get_planning_scene reports from the map, the objects and the robot's own body, the arms' links and objects from one another included; a state nearer than it is in collision, and one at a distance of 0 or less is in contact. Between an attached object and the links of the arm that carries it, outside its touch_links, the clearance is 0: they keep out of contact; from the rest of the robot, an attached object keeps the clearance as from an object. Objects one arm carries are never checked against each other. A pair is checked when one of its bodies moves: a link of an arm the path moves, or an object such a link carries; a pair whose bodies all stand still while another named arm moves, such as an arm that stays where it starts and the torso, is not checked, and when every named arm stays where it starts, the pairs of each are checked. A pair allowed to touch is never checked, and its members may overlap; so is a pair of the robot's own links that its model exempts, such as two adjacent links. A plan whose start is in contact fails with start_in_collision, and so does one whose start stands nearer than the clearance to the map or to an object no arm holds, as MoveIt's collision check, padded by the clearance, refuses it; the message names the nearest such pair and how far apart it stands. A start closer than the clearance within the robot's own body is valid when, until the clearance is reached, the most by which the robot falls short of it never grows, to the rounding of the arithmetic; a plan that cannot keep this fails with no_path. Between checked states, a path from a start less than 0.2 mm above the clearance from the map and the objects, or 0.4 mm above it from its own body, may come up to 0.1 mm or 0.2 mm below it respectively, and a path from a start nearer than the clearance within its own body stays above half the greatest distance it has reached. A Cartesian path that checks collisions refuses a start as a plan does. A start outside a joint limit by no more than the implementer's start tolerance is moved inside it; a plan or a Cartesian path whose start lies farther out is refused with precondition_failed. execute_joint_path runs a planned path from where the arms stand: given each arm's start_joint_positions of the plan as its expected_start_joint_positions, it refuses the path with precondition_failed unless each arm stands within limb_motion's start tolerance of them, and with rejected when the joint limits cannot run it within 60 s. limb_motion's guard checks the robot's own body with margins of its own, so execute_joint_path may still refuse a planned path with unreachable. Every tolerance and allowed_planning_time_s is above 0, and allowed_planning_time_s is at most 60. Any other value out of range, a start aside, which the start rule above judges, a name the robot or the scene does not have or that lies outside the named arms, an empty arms, an arm named twice, a joint vector that does not hold one value per joint of its arm, a goal with no constraint, a name given twice in one list of constraints, at least as many path orientation constraints on the arms the plan moves as those arms have joints, an arm whose goal constraints mix joint constraints with position or orientation constraints or name more than one of its links, in a check, arms with different numbers of waypoints or an arm with none, and, in a Cartesian path, no waypoints or a link other than the arm's grasp_link and the links fixed to it, are refused with rejected.",
      "The positions and orientations in the robot frame have the mark `robot_frame` (marks.json5). The workflow side reads it: a workflow passes a position or an orientation only from a field with this mark of a result or an observation of the same role, never as a literal.",
    ],
  },
  failure_kinds: {
    unreachable: "No joint positions that meet the goal without a collision were found in the time allowed",
    no_path: "Goal positions were found, but no path joined them in the time allowed, or none keeps the path orientations",
    start_in_collision: "The start touches an obstacle or the robot's own body in a pair that is checked, or stands nearer than the clearance to the map or an object no arm holds; the message names the pair, how far apart it stands, and what to do",
  },
  interfaces: {
    actions: [
      {
        name: "plan_joint_path",
        description: "Plans a joint path for the named arms from their start to a goal, choosing a route that avoids collisions, between the arms included. The goal holds at least one joint, position or orientation constraint of goal_joint_constraints, goal_position_constraints or goal_orientation_constraints. The goal constraints on one arm are joint constraints alone, or position and orientation constraints of one of its links alone; different arms may take different kinds. An arm whose goal constraints mix them, or whose goal position and orientation constraints name more than one of its links, is refused with rejected. An arm that no goal constraint names stays where it starts: each of its waypoints is its start. A joint or link the goal leaves free on an arm it constrains may end anywhere. A cancel ends the plan, and the goal ends cancelled.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            arms: {
              $type: "array",
              $description: "The arms to plan for, at least one.",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                arm_name: { $type: "string", $description: "The limb name." },
                start_joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "Where the arm's path starts; empty: where the arm stands." },
              },
            },
            goal_joint_constraints: {
              $type: "array",
              $description: "Targets for any of the joints of the arms; each joint may end tolerance_above above and tolerance_below below its target, in rad, or m for a prismatic joint. A target up to 0.001 outside its joint limits is taken at the limit, so a measured position sent back as a target is planned to; one farther out is refused with rejected.",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                joint_name: { $type: "string", $description: "As describe_arms names it." },
                position: "f64",
                tolerance_above: "f64",
                tolerance_below: "f64",
              },
            },
            goal_position_constraints: {
              $type: "array",
              $description: "Where the origin of a link of the arms must end: within tolerance_m (m) of position, the straight-line distance.",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                link_name: { $type: "string", $description: "As describe_arms names it, such as its grasp_link." },
                position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $marks: ["robot_frame"] },
                tolerance_m: "f64",
              },
            },
            goal_orientation_constraints: {
              $type: "array",
              $description: "How a link of the arms must end up turned.",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                link_name: "string",
                orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $marks: ["robot_frame"] },
                tolerance_rad: { $type: "f64", $description: "The largest angle (rad) of the rotation from orientation to the link's orientation." },
                free_axis: { $type: "string", $enum: ["none", "x", "y", "z"], $description: "\"none\": tolerance_rad bounds the whole rotation. \"x\", \"y\" or \"z\": that axis of the link's frame is held, either way along it, with the link free to turn about it, such as a gripper's approach axis; tolerance_rad then bounds the angle between that axis and its direction in orientation." },
              },
            },
            path_orientation_constraints: {
              $type: "array",
              $description: "Orientations held along the whole path, such as a carried cup kept upright, on any links of the arms: every state of the path from the plan's start, its rounded corners included, holds each. Run from within limb_motion's start tolerance of that start, a link turns from where the path holds it by at most the sum of its joints' differences from the start. Their order carries no meaning. Empty: the path holds no orientation. A goal that names a position of a link and no orientation takes the orientation of that link's constraint here. A start more than 0.99 of tolerance_rad from an orientation fails with no_path, and so does a goal farther from it than 0.9 of tolerance_rad or the start's own angle from it, whichever is more. An arm that stays where it starts holds its constraints when its start lies within tolerance_rad.",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                link_name: "string",
                orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $marks: ["robot_frame"] },
                tolerance_rad: { $type: "f64", $description: "The largest angle (rad) of the rotation from orientation to the link's orientation." },
                free_axis: { $type: "string", $enum: ["none", "x", "y", "z"], $description: "\"none\": tolerance_rad bounds the whole rotation. \"x\", \"y\" or \"z\": that axis of the link's frame is held, either way along it, with the link free to turn about it, such as a gripper's approach axis; tolerance_rad then bounds the angle between that axis and its direction in orientation." },
              },
            },
            objective: { $type: "string", $enum: ["any"], $description: "\"any\": the first valid path found, simplified in the time left." },
            allowed_planning_time_s: { $type: "f64", $description: "The time (s) the plan may take from when the implementer takes the goal: more than 0, and at most 60. The simplifier's first pass and the check of the path the robot runs run to their end, past it when the plan leaves them none." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            arms: {
              $type: "array",
              $description: "Each arm's path, in the order of the goal's arms: where it starts, and its waypoints after the start, at least one, as many for every arm. The arms pass their k-th waypoints together, and their last ones meet the goal.",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                arm_name: "string",
                start_joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "The start the plan used: the goal's, or where the arm stood, each joint outside a limit by no more than the implementer's start tolerance moved onto it." },
                waypoints: {
                  $type: "array",
                  $items: {
                    $type: "object",
                    joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
                    position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $marks: ["robot_frame"], $description: "The arm's grasp-point position here, and orientation its orientation, as in limb_state." },
                    orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $marks: ["robot_frame"] },
                  },
                },
              },
            },
            map_stamp: { $type: "time", $optional: true, $description: "The time of the newest depth frame the plan used; absent with no camera." },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["unreachable", "no_path", "start_in_collision"],
      },
      {
        name: "plan_cartesian_path",
        description: "Computes a joint path along which one arm's link follows straight lines, from where it stands through the given poses, its orientation turning by the shorter slerp in step with its position (a pose at the same position turns in place), within 1 mm and 0.01 rad at every state and between states. Returns as much of the path as is valid: it ends before a pose that inverse kinematics cannot reach, that collides where avoid_collisions is true, or past which the precision cannot be kept. Every state is within the joint limits. From a start closer than the clearance within the robot's own body, the path leaves in one straight joint run to the first state that keeps the clearance, and ends at its start where no state keeps it, or the run breaks the start rule or leaves the precision. A cancel ends the path, and the goal ends cancelled.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            arm_name: { $type: "string", $description: "The limb name." },
            start_joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "Where the path starts; empty: where the arm stands." },
            link_name: { $type: "string", $description: "The link that follows the lines, as describe_arms names it: the arm's grasp_link, or a link fixed to it." },
            waypoints: {
              $type: "array",
              $description: "The poses to pass through, at least one.",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $marks: ["robot_frame"] },
                orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $marks: ["robot_frame"] },
              },
            },
            avoid_collisions: { $type: "bool", $description: "If false, no collision is checked, the robot's own body included, and no depth frame is needed: a test of reach and precision alone, such as whether an obstacle is what blocks a path." },
          },
        },
        result_service: {
          response_message_format: {
            start_joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "The start the path used: the goal's, or where the arm stood, each joint outside a limit by no more than the implementer's start tolerance moved onto it." },
            waypoints: {
              $type: "array",
              $description: "As plan_joint_path gives an arm's; empty when not even the first step is valid.",
              $items: {
                $type: "object",
                joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
                position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $marks: ["robot_frame"], $description: "The arm's grasp-point position here, and orientation its orientation, as in limb_state." },
                orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $marks: ["robot_frame"] },
              },
            },
            fraction: { $type: "f64", $description: "The share of the requested path covered, 0 to 1: each line, the one from the start included, counts equally; a partial line counts the share of its length covered, or of its turn for a line that only turns; a line that neither moves nor turns counts whole once reached." },
            map_stamp: { $type: "time", $optional: true, $description: "The time of the newest depth frame the path used; absent with no camera, and with avoid_collisions false." },
          },
        },
        failure_kinds: ["start_in_collision"],
      },
    ],
    services: [
      {
        name: "check_joint_path",
        description: "Checks the path execute_joint_path would run from the start through the waypoints, for collisions and joint limits, as a plan is checked. Moves nothing. A start in contact or nearer than the clearance to the map or an object no arm holds, a start outside a joint limit by more than the implementer's start tolerance, a waypoint more than 0.001 outside a joint limit (one closer is taken at the limit, as execute_joint_path takes it), and a path that breaks the start rule each give clear false.",
        request_message_format: {
          arms: {
            $type: "array",
            $description: "The arms whose path to check, at least one, each with its own waypoints, as execute_joint_path takes them.",
            $items: {
              $type: "object",
              arm_name: "string",
              start_joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "Where the arm's path starts; empty: where the arm stands." },
              waypoints: {
                $type: "array",
                $description: "The positions after the start, at least one; every arm has as many.",
                $items: {
                  $type: "object",
                  joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
                },
              },
            },
          },
        },
        response_message_format: {
          clear: { $type: "bool", $description: "True when the whole path passes: no collision, every joint within its limits." },
          clear_waypoints: { $type: "u32", $description: "The most waypoints, from the first, whose path, every arm run together through them with the last of them as its end, passes; all of them when clear, and 0 when the start fails or the path to the first waypoints fails." },
          reason: { $type: "string", $description: "What fails, and how close it comes; empty when clear." },
          map_stamp: { $type: "time", $optional: true, $description: "The time of the newest depth frame the check used; absent with no camera." },
        },
      },
      {
        name: "describe_arms",
        description: "Each arm's joints and links, by the names that constraints and the planning scene use.",
        response_message_format: {
          arms: {
            $type: "array",
            $items: {
              $type: "object",
              name: { $type: "string", $description: "The limb name." },
              gripper_name: { $type: "string", $description: "The limb name of the arm's gripper." },
              joint_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "In limb_state's order, which is the order of a waypoint." },
              joint_lower_limits: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "Each joint's limits, as limb_motion enforces them, in the order of joint_names." },
              joint_upper_limits: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
              link_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "Every link of the arm, its gripper's included." },
              grasp_link: { $type: "string", $description: "The link at the grasp point." },
              approach_axis: { $type: "string", $enum: ["+x", "-x", "+y", "-y", "+z", "-z"], $description: "The axes of grasp_link's frame along which the gripper approaches an item and along which its jaws close." },
              closing_axis: { $type: "string", $enum: ["+x", "-x", "+y", "-y", "+z", "-z"] },
              gripper_links: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The gripper's links, which a held object may touch." },
            },
          },
          body_link_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The robot's links outside its arms, such as the torso." },
        },
      },
      {
        name: "clear_occupancy_map",
        description: "Empties the map; plans, Cartesian paths and checks that check collisions are then refused until the next depth frame.",
      },
      {
        name: "apply_collision_objects",
        description: "Adds, moves or removes objects, in order, all or none. \"add\" places an object with its shapes, replacing one of the same id and keeping its allowed pairs; \"move\" reads only id and pose; \"remove\" reads only id and drops every allowed pair that names it. Fields an operation does not read are not checked. An empty list changes nothing. An empty id, an id equal to a link name or to \"occupancy_map\", an unknown id for \"move\" or \"remove\", an attached object, an \"add\" with no shapes, and an open mesh are refused with rejected.",
        request_message_format: {
          objects: {
            $type: "array",
            $items: {
              $type: "object",
              id: "string",
              operation: { $type: "string", $enum: ["add", "move", "remove"] },
              position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $marks: ["robot_frame"] },
              orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $marks: ["robot_frame"] },
              shapes: {
                $type: "array",
                $items: {
                  $type: "object",
                  kind: { $type: "string", $enum: ["box", "sphere", "cylinder", "mesh"] },
                  dimensions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "Centered on the shape's pose: a box's full side lengths x, y, z; a sphere's radius; a cylinder's height along z, then radius (m), each above 0. Empty for a mesh." },
                  mesh_vertices: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "Three coordinates per vertex (m); empty for a primitive." },
                  mesh_triangles: { $type: "array", $items: "u32", $description: "Three 0-based vertex indices per triangle; the triangles close a solid, each edge bordering exactly two of them, and a link or an attached object inside it is in contact with it." },
                  position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $description: "The shape's pose in the object's frame." },
                  orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4 },
                },
              },
            },
          },
        },
      },
      {
        name: "apply_attached_collision_object",
        description: "Attaches an object of the scene to a link where it stands, or detaches it where it stands; its allowed pairs stay. An attached object moves with its link, and its pairs with that link and its touch_links are never checked. Attaching an attached object, or detaching one that is not attached, is refused with rejected; a handover detaches, then attaches. An attach before the arms' joint positions are measured is refused with precondition_failed. Fields detach does not read are not checked.",
        request_message_format: {
          object_id: "string",
          link_name: { $type: "string", $description: "An arm's grasp_link, as describe_arms names it." },
          touch_links: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "Links of the robot, as describe_arms names them, that may touch the object; an object id here is refused with rejected." },
          operation: { $type: "string", $enum: ["attach", "detach"] },
        },
      },
      {
        name: "set_allowed_collision",
        description: "Lets the object name, attached or not, touch each of other_names, or stops it: links, objects, or \"occupancy_map\" for the voxel map. A name that is not an object of the scene, and other_names holding name itself, are refused with rejected. A pair is unordered, and an empty other_names changes nothing. Pairs stay through attach, detach, move and a replacing add; removing an object drops every pair that names it. An attached object is never checked against its link and touch_links, whatever the pairs say.",
        request_message_format: {
          name: "string",
          other_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string" },
          allowed: "bool",
        },
      },
      {
        name: "get_planning_scene",
        description: "Everything the scene holds.",
        response_message_format: {
          objects: {
            $type: "array",
            $description: "The objects that no link carries, sorted by id.",
            $items: {
              $type: "object",
              id: "string",
              position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $marks: ["robot_frame"] },
              orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $marks: ["robot_frame"] },
              shapes: {
                $type: "array",
                $items: {
                  $type: "object",
                  kind: { $type: "string", $enum: ["box", "sphere", "cylinder", "mesh"] },
                  dimensions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
                  mesh_vertices: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
                  mesh_triangles: { $type: "array", $items: "u32" },
                  position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3 },
                  orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4 },
                },
              },
            },
          },
          attached_objects: {
            $type: "array",
            $description: "The objects a link carries, sorted by id, each posed in the frame of that link.",
            $items: {
              $type: "object",
              id: "string",
              link_name: "string",
              touch_links: { $type: "array", $items: "string" },
              position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3 },
              orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4 },
              shapes: {
                $type: "array",
                $items: {
                  $type: "object",
                  kind: { $type: "string", $enum: ["box", "sphere", "cylinder", "mesh"] },
                  dimensions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
                  mesh_vertices: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
                  mesh_triangles: { $type: "array", $items: "u32" },
                  position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3 },
                  orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4 },
                },
              },
            },
          },
          allowed_pairs: {
            $type: "array",
            $description: "The pairs set_allowed_collision allowed, each once, name_a before name_b in sort order, the pairs sorted.",
            $items: {
              $type: "object",
              name_a: "string",
              name_b: "string",
            },
          },
          clearance_m: { $type: "f64", $description: "The clearance (m) each state keeps from the map, the objects and the robot's own body; an attached object keeps it from all but the arm that carries it and the other objects that arm carries." },
          voxel_size_m: { $type: "f64", $description: "The side of the map's cubes (m), set at launch, with or without a camera." },
        },
      },
    ],
  },
}
